      "response": "## Investigation report\n\nCitation integrity checked against saved evidence. Human review is required to assess the findings.\n\n### 1. Docs · Low\n\nThe code imports the Streamlit library as the alias st\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_2a43b6ff45b2e46137ec6a7893043737\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 2. Docs · Low\n\nThe function load\\_rows is decorated with @st\\.cache\\_data\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_2a43b6ff45b2e46137ec6a7893043737\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 3. Docs · Low\n\nThe load\\_rows function returns the list \\[1, 2, 3\\]\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_2a43b6ff45b2e46137ec6a7893043737\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 4. Docs · Low\n\nThe script calls st\\.write with the result of load\\_rows\\(\\)\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_2a43b6ff45b2e46137ec6a7893043737\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### Missing information\n\n- Confirm whether the required credential is configured \\(yes/no\\); provide the provider name, configuration variable names, an endpoint without credentials or secret query parameters, and redacted error messages\\. Do not share credential values or other secrets\\.\n\n### Proposed next steps\n\n- Check that the @st\\.cache\\_data decorator does not cache any sensitive data and that the cached output is appropriate for the intended use\\.\n",
